{"name":"Introspective","hex":"#6d6053","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"introspective","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Examining one's own perceptions and sensory experiences; contemplative or thoughtful about oneself."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/introspective"}],"entries":[{"title":"Introspective","blocks":[{"text":"Introspective is the third studio album by English synth-pop duo Pet Shop Boys, released on 10 October 1988 by Parlophone. It received generally positive reviews from critics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1f/Introspective_%28Pet_Shop_Boys_album%29.jpg/330px-Introspective_%28Pet_Shop_Boys_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Introspective","wikidata":"Q928076"},{"title":"Introspective (Amber Smith album)","blocks":[{"text":"Introspective is the fourth studio album recorded by Amber Smith. The album was recorded at the Podium Studios in Budapest, Hungary in 2007. The album was mixed by Chris Brown, who previously worked on Radiohead's The Bends album, and it was mastered at Foon Mastering Studios in Belgium. The album was released by the Lithuanian label M.P.3 International as CD and digitally."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f2/Introspective_%28Amber_Smith_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Introspective_(Amber_Smith_album)","wikidata":"Q249919"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/57/Introspective_pet_shop_boys_vinyl_edition.jpg/500px-Introspective_pet_shop_boys_vinyl_edition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/57/Introspective_pet_shop_boys_vinyl_edition.jpg/1280px-Introspective_pet_shop_boys_vinyl_edition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org